{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact d2601775600a1d78a348b1c611ffda0100220b40 on request/i7-numeric-conversion-decision, sole changed path notes/2026-09-05-capability-context-contract.md, reporting artifact 9ca47165, under review request #4258 (2c6ba499) and source request #4252 (b7cf90a8), adopted proposal 607fcd01 ratified by hugh (ratifier) in the effective act cd4783f6. Reviewed in a detached checkout of my own at the exact head: one commit over main 62fde541, git diff --check clean, the frontmatter adds #4252 as a base, the history and cross-reference edits at lines 3, 51-56 and 136-137 are accurate (object-key landing at 62fde541 through receipt e73c4b74 and publication a1c97964, proposal 077daf8d, my approval of f0eed793), and every previous adopted section and the declaration through the eight gates are byte-identical to main. All 22 local links resolve in the checkout.\n\nConditions of #4252 and the adopted proposal, checked against the new section at lines 598-675: one portable signed64 rule (NaN to zero; at or above exact 2^63 including +Inf to MaxInt64; at or below exact -2^63 including -Inf to MinInt64; other finite values truncate toward zero, preserving fractional and negative-zero behaviour); comparison against the exactly representable powers of two before any native cast, with float64(MaxInt64) named as an unsafe inclusive bound; applied on all four 64-bit targets with no runtime architecture branch, no silent AMD64 selection, no blanket nonfinite refusal and no widening of the builtin set; the AMD64 change is disclosed as a deliberate choice of the observed ARM behaviour, not as existing portable semantics; operation-specific evaluation order, early returns and errors are kept; substring bound and round decimal-exponent arithmetic are signed64 with defined wrap; an invalid substring slice keeps a protected fatal failure at its existing semantic point, with no native bounds panic, no successful empty substitute and no ordinary error a preliminary group-key probe could swallow; the three named cases carry the required portable results ((1.25,0/0) -\u003e 1 against inferred 0; (\"abc\",0,1e300) -\u003e \"abc\" against inferred empty; (\"abc\",1,1e300) -\u003e retained failure against inferred empty); infinities, huge finite values, the signed64 boundaries and nearest representable neighbours, negative zero, fractional precision/start/length, huge exponent arithmetic, missing values and empty strings are covered with exact outputs or existing error classes and runtime error text is excluded as a criterion; predicate semantics are preserved ([1,2,3][0/0] keeps all items, [1,2,3][1/0] keeps D1001, finite out-of-input indices select nothing, floor before index); the rule is explicitly not applied to every floating intermediate or Go cast, and every excluded builtin cast needs a confinement reason; the complete reachable inventory across the admitted AST and callable routes including aliases, partials, compositions, closed matcher callbacks and helpers is required and attached; native pinned, private native and controlled-overlay evidence and the instruction-level Intel inference are kept separate and the absence of AMD64 execution and full host replay is stated; gate 3 is extended with paired output/error/ordered-call/accounting cases, at-bound/one-over outcomes and omission controls that restore a native cast, omit a guard or remove a charge, with the ARM-only limitation of native-cast restoration recorded and the cross-target proof required before admission; identity accounting names core.jsonata, grammar/dialect and corpus/version components, keeps exactly ten components and old-identity recognition, revalidates stored programs before replay writes with refusal leaving projection and frontier unchanged, keeps the acknowledged reset boundary, four stages and eight gates; no publication, admission, live operation, reset, migration or release is authorized; implementation, pin and callers stay on #4043. The pending-adoption wording at line 3 predates Hugh's adoption and is retained at the requester's instruction.\n\nEvidence, independently verified rather than counted. (1) I re-ran the attached native-probe.go in a fresh module pinned to github.com/jsonata-go/jsonata v0.0.0-20250709164031-599f35f32e5f on darwin/arm64 with Go 1.27.0: all 174 outputs and error strings match native-results.jsonl, and the table's thirteen expressions produce exactly the pinned values or failures the note attributes to ARM (1, \"abc\", the slice-bounds runtime error, \"bc\", 1.2, \"b\", null, null, [1,2,3], D1001, null, null, 2). The native group probe reproduces the raw slice-bounds panic escaping through a group key on pinned 599f. (2) I ran the signed replay-numeric-evidence.py with the retained immutable 311d9afc checkout and the tailapp core at 62fde541 into my own output directory; it asserted the 311d head, wrote only overlay and experiment files, and left both checkouts clean. Its private-native and private-portable logs match the signed private-native-results.json and private-portable-results.json exactly for every case: outputs, errors, ordered builtin call traces, used work/allocation totals and the three bound outcomes; all 156 successful portable cases succeed at the exact bound and refuse with resource_work or resource_allocation one unit short, and the 18 failures are the expected ones. The five controlled mutations fail as recorded (Intel-style conversion returns 0 for (1.25,0/0); skipped charge passes work-one-short; missing NaN predicate classification refuses [1,2,3][0/0] with resource_contract; omitted slice guard reaches the native bounds panic; ordinary-error substitution lets the group probe swallow the failure), the two controls pass, and native-cast restoration survives on this ARM host exactly as the note discloses. The private 311d NaN-predicate gap reproduces as the single native-private mismatch and is confined to the evidence overlay and listed as a #4043 obligation, not hidden. (3) I re-ran conversion-inventory.go with GOWORK=off CGO_ENABLED=0 from the 311d root: 63 production files and 208 integer-target sites, matching typed-conversions.json; the inventory assesses all 34 float-source routes individually with a classification and a reachability reason (3 portable semantic conversions at substring start/length and round precision; 4 legacy finite index routes converging on the bounded private predicate path; 4 legacy matcher bookkeeping sites eliminated on the private contains path; 9 excluded datetime/integer-format closures; 9 excluded builtin closures for pad/match/replace/split/formatNumber/formatBase absent from the immutable 19-builtin dispatcher; 2 excluded generated ranges refused at lexical admission; 1 excluded fromMillis callback; 1 fixed package-initialization conversion; 1 finite input-bounded filter index), and its reachability closure covers the AST dispatcher, the 19 callable identities with aliases, partials, compositions, transforms and closed contains callbacks. (4) Instruction evidence: the four Go 1.26.7 build listings show FCVTZSD on arm64 and CVTTSD2SQ on amd64 at the round-precision cast; the Intel SDM reference supports the masked NaN integer-indefinite inference; the note states this is not AMD64 execution. (5) Provenance: the artifact's eighteen actual bases are the #4252 promise 661a0721, the published note a1c97964 and the sixteen implementation artifacts in source-provenance.json; all sixteen are live and fresh and each file is byte-identical at d2601775 to the commit its artifact names. No statement after the review request names this head other than my promise.\n\nArchitecture: affected layers are the jsonataddl evaluator layer (compile, confine, evaluate, identity, dialect, input contract, load, values, authorizer, application), the engine and projection layer above it, and the MCP tools surface; the exact head changes documentation only and preserves every implemented contract, so no reference page needs a contract update. The decision fixes the semantics of three reachable float-to-integer conversions and the invalid-slice failure class; the private 311d evaluator does not yet implement it and the note says so.\n\nSecurity: adoption basis is sound (proposal 607fcd01 rests on the artifact and was ratified by hugh, who holds ratifier, in cd4783f6; the review follows adoption and asks for decision review only). Untrusted numbers from expressions (NaN, infinities, values beyond 2^63) are bounded before any native cast by comparison with exact powers of two, closing the implementation-defined Go conversion and the amd64 integer-indefinite path; saturation to MaxInt64/MinInt64 is well defined and the downstream signed64 wrap is declared rather than assumed; the invalid-slice case is a fatal contract failure rather than an ordinary error, which matters because the object-key preliminary probe swallows ordinary errors, and the group probe evidence shows the raw panic that the rule prevents; predicate classification precedes conversion so NaN cannot become an index; every excluded cast has a reachability reason instead of a grep result; selected-extension confinement is unchanged; the limits of the evidence (no AMD64 execution, no full host replay, native-cast restoration surviving ARM-only tests, provisional logical resource units) are stated and the cross-target proof stays a #4043 admission obligation. No unresolved security defect.\n\nSimplification: one explicit rule, a nine-row table of changed and unchanged cases, and references to the shared gates, with the inventory and controls in attachments as the conditions require; the closing identity and gates paragraph repeats the closers of the earlier amendments, which keeps each amendment self-contained. Nothing to cut without weakening the conditions.\n\nApproval applies only to this exact head and named artifact. Builder ratifies this verdict and seals the approved head with path succession, push, CI and